\ prog/wm.fam — the window manager, in embryo: the HTTP and WebSocket server
\ (prog/http.fam), the page's store box (lib/pkv.fam) and its terminals
\ (lib/pterm.fam: a shell per socket, piped through the store), as a program holding
\ TCP port 8080.  It is what src/kernel.fam used to serve from the kernel.
\ Built with lib/pnet.fam, src/eth.fam, src/ip.fam, src/udp.fam, src/tcp.fam,
\ lib/pstack.fam, lib/pkv.fam and prog/http.fam (scripts/build.sh).  Later it
\ owns windows and binds other programs' handle 0 to them.
\ tmturn ( -- )  every terminal whose out key was written (wbit: all are marked)
\ gets what is new relayed to its socket as a "term:" frame; one that does not
\ fit now stays marked for the next turn.  A shell that has ended closes its terminal.
: tmb variable ;  : tmblk variable ;
: tmturn
	20 lit 0 lit do
		i tment @ ?dup if i tment 8 lit + @ if
			tmb @ 5 lit + tmblk @ !  600 lit tmblk @ 4 lit + !  i tment 4 lit + @ tmblk @ 8 lit + !
			i 1 lit tmkey tmblk @ sread dup 0 lit u> if
				i hslot hsel
				hs @ 10 lit + @ 0=  hc @ tcproom over 9 lit + u< 0= and if                 \ room on the socket now
					dup i tment 4 lit + dup @ rot + swap !
					"term:" tmb @ 5 lit mcopy  tmb @ swap 5 lit + 1 lit wsend
				else drop then
			else drop  0 lit i tment 8 lit + !
				tstate 0= if i hslot hsel  "term:\n[the shell has ended]\n" dup slen 1 lit wsend  i termclos then
			then
		else drop then then
	loop ;

40 lit pstack
6 lit 1F90 lit pbind ?dup if "wm: cannot hold TCP port 8080: " puts u. '\n' lit putc texit then
20 lit tcpinit  -1 lit kvinit  terminit  1F90 lit 20 lit httpinit  620 lit alloc tmb !  10 lit alloc tmblk !
"wm: serving http on port 8080\n" puts
begin
	nbit wbit or F4240 lit wait                   \ frames, a watched key, or 100 ms for the timers
	wbit and if 20 lit 0 lit do i tment @ if -1 lit i tment 8 lit + ! then loop then
	begin netrx while pnetin netrel repeat
	httpturn
	tmturn
	tcptick
0 lit until
